Reason :

AEMO ELECTRICITY MARKET NOTICE

Australian Services Union (ASU) members are currently engaged in Protected Industrial Action in support of fair wages and conditions. As a result of this action there may be intermittent disruption to some services. ASU members remain committed to the safe operation of the network. We hope for a quick resolution to negotiations and the resumption of normal operations.

AEMO declares a Forecast LOR2 condition under clause 4.8.4(b) of the National Electricity Rules for the TAS region for the following period[s]:

[1.] From 0830 hrs 20/11/2026 to 0900 hrs 20/11/2026.         
The forecast capacity reserve requirement is  438 MW.
The minimum capacity reserve available is 434 MW.

AEMO is seeking a market response.

For more information on forecast reserve conditions, refer to: https://www.aemo.com.au/nem/reserve_conditions

Manager NEM Real Time Operations

